	abstract = {The present competitive market environment imposes new challenges to the food-processing sector such as the availability of the logistic facility, procurement facilities, sequencing, and random layout changes that create the need for a full-scale scheduling approach along with sequential operations. Building upon the Mixed Integer Linear Programming (MILP), this study provides an extension to the mathematical formulation of optimal production scheduling problems for the ice cream industry as an example of a complex and fast-moving food-processing industry. The extension developed in this paper aims to mathematically formulate and solve an integrated problem involving procurement strategy and vehicle routing problem (VRP) in a medium-scale ice cream industry considering industrial symbiosis opportunities between plants and interval and sequence variables with various constraints. The results enabled the optimization of the make-span time including procurement periods and vehicle routing problems and propose a strategic model to guide decision-making in production planning and scheduling. © 2023 IEEE.},
